WEBVTT

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:32.033
Enemy Notos fleet is
spreading out on our port side!

00:00:32.283 --> 00:00:33.951
Enemy fleet is opening fire!

00:00:34.202 --> 00:00:37.413
2nd and 3rd Armored Fleets have been trapped!

00:00:37.663 --> 00:00:40.458
Enemy is outside our main fleet's firing range!

00:00:40.708 --> 00:00:42.919
2nd Armored Fleet is taking damage!

00:00:43.169 --> 00:00:46.464
Flanking both sides and then striking the rear...

00:00:46.714 --> 00:00:48.716
Exactly by the book.

00:00:48.966 --> 00:00:53.304
It seems the Notos commander
is fond of tried-and-true tactics.

00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:54.889
They're surrounding us!

00:01:31.384 --> 00:01:35.137
Hmm. Now that's an impressive retreat.

00:01:35.388 --> 00:01:39.850
It appears your little act was convincing,
firang, despite your lack of wit.

00:01:40.101 --> 00:01:44.272
You're late. You're tarnishing
your swift reputation, Sorfish!

00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:48.109
Now hear this! All ships, bring about!

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:50.069
Counter-envelop the enemy!

00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:51.320
Gloria!

00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:55.199
Teach these repatriates the glory
of the Augusta's soldiers!

00:01:55.449 --> 00:01:57.451
Gloria, Augusta!

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:03.958
Show these Notos returnees why
our fleet is known as "The Swift"!

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:06.544
Gloria, Augusta!

00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:35.239
Enemy ships out of sight.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:37.158
Enemy ships out of sight!

00:02:37.408 --> 00:02:40.202
Any further pursuit would be meaningless.

00:02:40.453 --> 00:02:41.579
All ships, change course!

00:02:41.829 --> 00:02:43.205
We're returning to the capital!

00:02:43.456 --> 00:02:45.291
Gloria!

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:58.262
Silvius, the Reaper...

00:02:58.346 --> 00:03:04.935
<i>No matter what might await us there</i>

00:03:05.186 --> 00:03:13.611
<i>I'll go to unexplored territory with you</i>

00:03:21.869 --> 00:03:29.919
<i>I just had a short dream</i>

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:34.548
<i>In it, I saw your back</i>

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:40.721
<i>Was it the past? The future?</i>

00:03:40.971 --> 00:03:51.482
<i>Ignore the needle on that meter
pointing to the red zone</i>

00:03:51.732 --> 00:03:54.610
<i>And go where the tailwinds
and your feelings point you</i>

00:03:54.860 --> 00:04:00.783
<i>Every time I flap my wings, it makes me realize</i>

00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:06.330
<i>That there are skies
I'll never be able to see again</i>

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:11.836
<i>But if you still want to take flight</i>

00:04:12.086 --> 00:04:18.634
<i>Then I will be your wings</i>

00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:50.374
firang of the 3rd Fleet
and Sorfish of the 4th Fleet

00:04:50.624 --> 00:04:52.168
<i>have destroyed the Notes ships.</i>

00:04:52.418 --> 00:04:54.462
Cleanup operations are now underway.

00:04:54.712 --> 00:04:57.131
Okay. What about Sadri?

00:04:57.381 --> 00:05:00.551
The 1st Fleet has subdued
the Corbeau Peninsula

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:04.138
and is now in pursuit of a
battleship of unknown affiliation...

00:05:07.016 --> 00:05:11.395
We have returned from Turan, Augusta!

00:05:11.645 --> 00:05:13.606
Luscinia!

00:05:13.856 --> 00:05:14.815
Welcome back!

00:05:15.065 --> 00:05:17.234
Thanks for all your hard work!

00:05:17.485 --> 00:05:18.360
Thank you!

00:05:18.611 --> 00:05:23.073
My deepest apologies for the fleet
you so graciously granted us...

00:05:23.324 --> 00:05:28.245
Don't look so down. I know you
did your very best, Kayvén.

00:05:28.496 --> 00:05:30.915
Thank you, Augusta...

00:05:31.165 --> 00:05:35.503
Umm... Kayvén. Can you
do that thing again today?

00:05:35.753 --> 00:05:38.380
Yes! Of course!

00:05:38.631 --> 00:05:42.384
Oh, please be careful, Augusta.
You mustn't frolic so...

00:05:42.635 --> 00:05:44.929
Vasant! Do you honestly think I would commit

00:05:45.179 --> 00:05:48.766
such a grievous blunder
as dropping the Augusta?!

00:05:53.437 --> 00:05:55.898
The cities of Turan have begun
to surrender one after another

00:05:56.148 --> 00:06:00.236
upon receiving word of lglasia's downfall.

00:06:00.486 --> 00:06:02.112
It appears an imperial edict
had been issued in advance,

00:06:02.363 --> 00:06:05.658
emphasizing immediate surrender and
the avoidance of prolonged fighting

00:06:05.908 --> 00:06:08.452
should the royal city fall.

00:06:08.702 --> 00:06:12.164
The king of Turan was known
for being a sensible moderate.

00:06:12.414 --> 00:06:16.544
Plus, they stood no chance
against the might of an Exile.

00:06:16.794 --> 00:06:20.422
Indeed. To think that they possess such power...

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:24.760
The Exiles...

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:29.515
The accursed return ships that
brought them to our world uninvited...

00:06:29.765 --> 00:06:35.104
With its role long fulfilled and its existence
fading from the returnees' memories,

00:06:35.354 --> 00:06:37.731
an Exile itself dealt them a crushing blow.

00:06:37.982 --> 00:06:43.320
For there is not yet enough abundance
in this world to accommodate all.

00:06:44.363 --> 00:06:49.118
Merely locating the Exile keys
continues to confound us;

00:06:49.368 --> 00:06:53.122
where did Your Majesty acquire
information about the Turan key?

00:06:53.372 --> 00:06:57.960
That is of no concern to us
rank and file soldiers, Vasant.

00:06:59.336 --> 00:07:04.967
Who used to live in the area we call Turan now?

00:07:05.217 --> 00:07:08.137
Ah. That territory was originally
inhabited by the tribe of people

00:07:08.387 --> 00:07:13.392
now residing in the northeastern
Gonia region of the Federation.

00:07:13.642 --> 00:07:20.024
Records indicate the Turans usurped their
land when they returned 118 years ago.

00:07:20.274 --> 00:07:23.944
Life in Gonia must be difficult
after last year's long cold spell.

00:07:24.194 --> 00:07:27.990
Please give their land of wheat
back to them soon, okay?

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.576
You are most kind, Augusta.

00:07:30.826 --> 00:07:33.787
We will do our utmost so that they
may receive the blessing of their land

00:07:34.038 --> 00:07:36.123
as quickly as possible.

00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:41.337
Our next topic is the ten-year
anniversary memorial service

00:07:41.587 --> 00:07:45.299
for the previous Augusta,
to be held next month...

00:07:45.549 --> 00:07:51.555
Oh, yes. It's already been ten
years since the Grand Race...

00:07:53.307 --> 00:07:55.184
Mother...

00:08:08.739 --> 00:08:09.782
Why?!

00:08:10.032 --> 00:08:12.701
Why didn't you save my sister?!

00:08:12.951 --> 00:08:15.871
You could've just left me there!

00:08:16.121 --> 00:08:19.375
Why me, instead of her...?!

00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:20.501
Why?!

00:08:20.751 --> 00:08:22.252
Please calm down, Princess Millia!

00:08:22.503 --> 00:08:24.755
--Let go!
--| know how you feel!

00:08:25.005 --> 00:08:29.385
But... we had no other choice at the time...

00:08:29.635 --> 00:08:34.181
What would you know?!
My sister absolutely must survive!

00:08:34.431 --> 00:08:36.767
She must, for Turan...

00:08:43.899 --> 00:08:46.652
Princess Millia! Princess Millia!

00:08:49.196 --> 00:08:50.072
Fam.

00:08:50.322 --> 00:08:51.699
Yeah.

00:08:51.949 --> 00:08:53.575
Shouldn't we do something?

00:08:53.826 --> 00:08:55.953
Let 'em be.

00:08:56.203 --> 00:08:59.665
Damn, what is that bird-brained
Federation thinking,

00:08:59.915 --> 00:09:01.667
dropping moons on us like that?!

00:09:01.917 --> 00:09:04.044
You mean "Exiles."

00:09:04.294 --> 00:09:08.882
They say our ancestors
rode 'em back here long ago.

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:11.051
Almost too crazy to believe...

00:09:16.390 --> 00:09:18.726
Haven't had such heavy trading in so long!

00:09:18.976 --> 00:09:21.437
Not since the fall of Met6pon, I think?

00:09:21.687 --> 00:09:22.980
The Lasas?

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:26.692
90,000? I'd say 50,000 at best
for something this banged up.

00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:29.653
--80,000!
--55,000!

00:09:29.903 --> 00:09:32.156
Our Turan...

00:09:32.406 --> 00:09:35.075
Our proud Turan warriors...

00:09:37.411 --> 00:09:41.331
Oh! Now that's a nice Unit! I'd expect
no less from the Turan flagship!

00:09:41.582 --> 00:09:43.625
Keep going! Keep going! Keep going!

00:09:43.876 --> 00:09:48.130
--Keep going! Keep going! Keep going!
--Hey! Make way! Coming through!

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.132
What a haul!

00:09:51.425 --> 00:09:53.886
--Wow! This is some great stuff!
--Whadya think?

00:09:54.136 --> 00:09:55.888
Yeah, just got it in.

00:09:56.138 --> 00:09:57.639
This is nice!

00:10:07.024 --> 00:10:10.235
Okay. Just lemme know
if you want anything else.

00:10:10.486 --> 00:10:12.362
Sure thing. Good tailwinds.

00:10:12.613 --> 00:10:14.406
May the wind carry your wings.

00:10:14.656 --> 00:10:16.617
Hold on! Wait!

00:10:23.499 --> 00:10:25.000
Wait!

00:10:41.016 --> 00:10:43.018
I'm back!

00:10:43.268 --> 00:10:44.937
You can relax here for now.

00:10:45.187 --> 00:10:46.647
Right!

00:10:46.897 --> 00:10:49.191
--Whee!
--Look out!

00:10:49.441 --> 00:10:53.487
Rene'! How many times have I said
not to ride the Melitta indoors?!

00:10:53.737 --> 00:10:56.031
Ghost ships come for
naughty children, you know!

00:10:56.281 --> 00:11:00.202
--'Kay...
--Welcome home, Sis!

00:11:00.452 --> 00:11:01.453
I'm back!

00:11:01.703 --> 00:11:04.915
Who's he? A new friend?!

00:11:05.165 --> 00:11:06.625
A friend?!

00:11:07.709 --> 00:11:10.212
9h, my! Oh, my!

00:11:10.462 --> 00:11:15.050
I heard everything! It must've been
hard on you! You're a real trouper!

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.720
--You really are!
--You're scaring Teddy, Mom.

00:11:18.971 --> 00:11:21.557
Oh, my! I'm sorry!

00:11:22.766 --> 00:11:24.309
Sorry it's such a mess.

00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:27.813
I'll go steam us some potatoes.
Make yourself at home.

00:11:28.939 --> 00:11:32.901
U-Umm, might I ask for a bit of water?

00:11:47.916 --> 00:11:53.922
Do not cry. You are our only hope, Millia.

00:11:54.172 --> 00:11:58.385
You are Turan's only hope, and mine...

00:11:58.635 --> 00:12:01.179
Please! Save my sister!

00:12:02.264 --> 00:12:03.807
I beg of you...!

00:12:12.649 --> 00:12:14.818
Fam! Come quick!

00:12:22.534 --> 00:12:24.953
That's dangerous! Come down, okay?

00:12:25.203 --> 00:12:28.832
Activate it by accident and
you'll cause a heap of trouble!

00:12:29.082 --> 00:12:31.251
Don't tell me what to do!

00:12:31.501 --> 00:12:33.462
I'm a Turan princess, you know!

00:12:33.712 --> 00:12:36.548
You've never touched a
Vespa in your life, Princess.

00:12:36.798 --> 00:12:39.176
You can't fly it! It's too much for you!

00:12:39.426 --> 00:12:42.804
Just give it up and come down from there!

00:12:43.055 --> 00:12:46.224
But... It belongs to my sister...

00:12:46.475 --> 00:12:48.352
It belongs to my sister...

00:12:49.937 --> 00:12:51.563
Get out of there!

00:12:52.648 --> 00:12:53.649
Get out!

00:12:53.899 --> 00:12:54.775
Absolutely not!

00:12:55.025 --> 00:12:56.318
Don't get the wrong idea!

00:12:56.568 --> 00:12:59.196
I want you to get out and move to the back seat!

00:12:59.446 --> 00:13:00.906
Hurry!

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.409
I'll be your wings!

00:13:09.831 --> 00:13:13.251
She has a big lead on us.

00:13:13.502 --> 00:13:15.712
I don't think we'll be able to spot her...

00:13:17.881 --> 00:13:20.342
Hey, you saw her Vanship, right?

00:13:20.592 --> 00:13:24.304
What did it look like?
Any special markings or colors?

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.265
--It doesn't matter...
--Huh?!

00:13:27.516 --> 00:13:29.518
It doesn't matter anymore...

00:13:29.768 --> 00:13:33.355
How can you say that?
It's important to you, isn't it?

00:13:33.605 --> 00:13:35.941
It's pointless.

00:13:36.191 --> 00:13:39.194
I can't do anything.

00:13:39.444 --> 00:13:45.158
I can't even recover my
sister's memento by myself...

00:13:45.409 --> 00:13:48.870
I'm completely useless...

00:13:53.667 --> 00:13:55.293
Pull it, Millia!

00:13:55.544 --> 00:13:57.212
The right lever!

00:13:57.462 --> 00:13:58.880
Like this?

00:14:10.183 --> 00:14:14.521
Wow, that's so neat.

00:14:14.771 --> 00:14:18.817
So this is what Turans use to make tea...

00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:20.902
Wow!

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.531
Here you go!

00:14:24.781 --> 00:14:27.409
Thank you...

00:14:27.659 --> 00:14:31.079
Have you always lived here?

00:14:31.329 --> 00:14:36.334
No, this is just one of several
bases we move to every so often.

00:14:36.585 --> 00:14:39.546
Most of the Skyfish we catch
belong to the Federation,

00:14:39.796 --> 00:14:42.382
so they're always watching for us.

00:14:42.632 --> 00:14:45.927
--Doesn't that make you afraid?
“Sometimes.

00:14:46.178 --> 00:14:50.515
But every one of us has fled here
to escape the Federation.

00:14:50.766 --> 00:14:52.726
To escape?

00:14:52.976 --> 00:14:55.353
People drift here after the
Federation destroys their homelands

00:14:55.604 --> 00:14:58.815
and they have nowhere to return to.

00:14:59.066 --> 00:15:05.155
So now there are lots and lots
of Sky Pirates all over the world...

00:15:05.405 --> 00:15:11.453
It happened to us too. I came to
Kartoffel when I was just a baby, though.

00:15:11.703 --> 00:15:13.622
Fam too?

00:15:13.872 --> 00:15:15.749
Wait!

00:15:21.129 --> 00:15:23.673
It's great that she gave it back so nicely!

00:15:23.924 --> 00:15:27.928
Even Sky Pirates will sympathize
with you if you explain things to them.

00:15:28.178 --> 00:15:31.765
But you'll need to give her
something in exchange later.

00:15:32.015 --> 00:15:34.851
The best way to repay a favor
is during a job, though.

00:15:35.102 --> 00:15:36.895
--I'm sorry.
--Huh?

00:15:37.145 --> 00:15:38.396
It's my fault...

00:15:38.647 --> 00:15:42.651
I'm completely useless and
cause nothing but trouble...

00:15:42.901 --> 00:15:45.821
"May the wind carry wings that are lost."

00:15:46.071 --> 00:15:51.827
Help anyone in the sky who needs help.
That's a Sky Pirate rule.

00:15:52.077 --> 00:15:56.039
They helped me too, in fact.
That's why I'm here today.

00:15:56.289 --> 00:15:59.501
They helped you...?

00:15:59.751 --> 00:16:02.087
They took me in.

00:16:08.093 --> 00:16:11.012
--Hey!
--Hey!

00:16:11.263 --> 00:16:13.348
You all right?!

00:16:14.850 --> 00:16:17.435
I'm sure it crashed right around here...

00:16:17.686 --> 00:16:19.229
There!

00:16:22.399 --> 00:16:24.067
Too late...

00:16:28.738 --> 00:16:30.866
Hey...

00:16:31.116 --> 00:16:32.284
Hey!

00:16:32.534 --> 00:16:33.785
Atamora! Come here!

00:16:34.035 --> 00:16:35.745
Huh? What is it?

00:16:37.122 --> 00:16:39.082
A baby's crying!

00:16:50.427 --> 00:16:52.095
I'm sorry.

00:16:52.345 --> 00:16:54.431
I only thought of myself...

00:16:54.681 --> 00:16:57.434
I thought I was the only one
who was sad and suffering...

00:16:57.684 --> 00:17:03.440
But they-- and you--
carry sadness and pain, too...

00:17:05.525 --> 00:17:09.779
To be honest, I do feel sad about it.

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:14.576
But it doesn't bother me much, since I
was too little to remember anything.

00:17:14.826 --> 00:17:18.121
Plus Gisey and her family
have always been there for me.

00:17:18.371 --> 00:17:21.041
Sky Pirates are kinda like one big family!

00:17:21.291 --> 00:17:22.834
I feel like as long as I'm in the sky,

00:17:23.084 --> 00:17:26.671
I'll always come across people who know me!

00:17:29.633 --> 00:17:32.010
Besides, I have a dream!

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:33.720
A dream?

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.352
Grand Race?

00:17:40.602 --> 00:17:44.314
It might've been just before you were born.

00:17:44.564 --> 00:17:49.402
Dad took Fam and me to see it.

00:17:49.653 --> 00:17:54.407
Vanship pilots from around the world
gathered and held an amazing race!

00:17:54.658 --> 00:17:59.621
It was to commemorate the day the Federation
and all the nations agreed to peace.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:04.125
Another Grand Race...?

00:18:04.376 --> 00:18:07.128
Yeah. Vanship pilots from around the world

00:18:07.379 --> 00:18:10.757
will gather and race again, just like that day!

00:18:11.007 --> 00:18:15.804
Sky Pirates, surface dwellers, everyone!
All soaring through the same sky!

00:18:16.054 --> 00:18:17.347
Doesn't that sound great?!

00:18:17.597 --> 00:18:21.351
But I'll be the winner, of course!

00:18:21.601 --> 00:18:24.020
Yes. That does sound splendid.

00:18:24.271 --> 00:18:25.730
Doesn't it, though?

00:18:28.692 --> 00:18:32.195
But, after that race, didn't...?

00:18:32.445 --> 00:18:38.076
Yeah. The peace fell apart in the end,
and there was never another race.

00:18:38.326 --> 00:18:40.412
All the Vanship pilots from around the world

00:18:40.662 --> 00:18:43.873
split up and left for their own skies...

00:18:44.124 --> 00:18:46.668
Wait, if the victory cup is here,

00:18:46.918 --> 00:18:48.753
does that mean the winner
of the Grand Race was...?!

00:18:49.004 --> 00:18:51.256
--It's time.
--Dad!

00:18:51.506 --> 00:18:54.467
--You all set?
--Yeah!

00:18:54.718 --> 00:18:56.928
All right! Let's go!

00:18:57.178 --> 00:18:59.556
People from around the world gathering

00:18:59.806 --> 00:19:03.059
and smiling into a peaceful sky free of fighting...

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:05.645
Oh, how wonderful that would be...

00:19:05.895 --> 00:19:09.024
We're gonna make it happen!
Someday, for sure!

00:19:09.274 --> 00:19:10.734
Yes...

00:19:33.923 --> 00:19:35.884
What's that, Fam?

00:19:36.134 --> 00:19:37.719
A farewell bonfire.

00:19:39.429 --> 00:19:41.431
That's a Turan ship...!

00:19:46.269 --> 00:19:49.230
"Return fallen wings to the sky."

00:19:49.481 --> 00:19:52.150
That's another Sky Pirate rule.

00:20:20.804 --> 00:20:26.851
May the lost souls safely return
to the far reaches of the sky...

00:20:29.187 --> 00:20:32.774
"Ola kae... Tode tai."

00:20:34.317 --> 00:20:36.861
Live with this ship in the sky.

00:20:37.112 --> 00:20:39.447
Living in the sky is our duty.

00:20:39.697 --> 00:20:41.866
Good tailwinds...

00:20:42.117 --> 00:20:43.993
Good tailwinds.

00:20:46.413 --> 00:20:49.958
I pray for tailwinds to
carry you through the sky.

00:21:01.261 --> 00:21:04.514
Ola kae. Tode tai.

00:21:06.307 --> 00:21:10.353
Ola kae. Tode tai.

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.169
Here.

00:21:34.419 --> 00:21:35.587
Thanks.

00:21:35.837 --> 00:21:37.630
You're welcome.

00:21:49.100 --> 00:21:52.520
It's delicious as always.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:54.772
Th-Thank you!

00:21:55.023 --> 00:21:57.192
I need to be strong too.

00:22:01.279 --> 00:22:05.283
Listen to this, Fam! I got some interesting info!

00:22:05.533 --> 00:22:09.537
Your "interesting info"
always ends up being lousy.

00:22:09.787 --> 00:22:14.501
The infamous Silvius was
spotted at the Miran lookout!

00:22:19.255 --> 00:22:20.798
Gisey! Millia!

00:22:21.049 --> 00:22:24.677
Wh... What's going on?

00:22:24.928 --> 00:22:29.098
I'm gonna go steal Silvius
the Reaper for Millia now!

00:22:31.142 --> 00:22:36.481
<i>How high are the skies,</i>

00:22:36.731 --> 00:22:42.529
<i>how strong are the winds,</i>

00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:48.368
<i>how clear are the waters</i>

00:22:48.618 --> 00:22:55.667
<i>you hold in your heart?</i>

00:22:56.876 --> 00:23:08.346
<i>One day I want to be the palm
of your hand and catch your tears</i>

00:23:08.596 --> 00:23:20.441
<i>I want us to share the
same sorrows, the same air</i>

00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:26.281
<i>I'll point the prow of this departing ship</i>

00:23:26.531 --> 00:23:35.081
<i>Right your way with no hesitation</i>

00:23:35.331 --> 00:23:41.045
<i>Let's raise the mast in this sea of wind</i>

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:46.843
<i>And set sail on these waves of clouds</i>

00:23:47.093 --> 00:23:52.599
<i>With the faraway stars for a compass</i>

00:23:52.849 --> 00:24:00.523
<i>I'll head beyond the horizon with you</i>

00:24:04.235 --> 00:24:06.029
<i>Your bag was a real surprise, Teddy!</i>

00:24:06.279 --> 00:24:09.699
<i>I wondered why it was so big, but I
never imagined it had an entire tea set!</i>

00:24:09.949 --> 00:24:14.203
<i>Yes! Serving the princess tea at a
moment's notice is a critical job of mine!</i>

00:24:14.454 --> 00:24:17.582
<i>Wow! Being the princess of
a kingdom sure has its perks!</i>

00:24:17.832 --> 00:24:19.375
<i>--So, what else?
--What do you mean?</i>

00:24:19.626 --> 00:24:21.502
<i>You know, what else do
you do besides serving tea?</i>

00:24:21.753 --> 00:24:24.839
<i>Are you like, "I'll protect you,
Princess!" when she's in danger?!</i>

00:24:25.089 --> 00:24:26.883
Uhh... Just tea.

00:24:27.133 --> 00:24:28.718
<i>Just tea?</i>
